Error [E0068]: This callable uses the retired result-arrow shape.
  --> tests/ui/loop_stream_reuse.jet:1:18
    |
  1 | fn count(n: Int) => Stream<Int> {
    |                  ^^
 Why: a return type sits after the parameter list, and `->` introduces the body; an effect ceiling follows the return type
 Fix: write `fn name(...) Type -> body`, or `fn name(...) Type -[Effects]> { … }`

Error [E0080]: A braced callable with a non-unit success result needs `->` before its body.
  --> tests/ui/loop_stream_reuse.jet:1:33
    |
  1 | fn count(n: Int) => Stream<Int> {
    |                                 ^
 Why: The body arrow marks a declared success value; unit and unit-fallible callables keep bare braces.
 Fix: Write `fn name(...) Type -> { ... }`; keep `fn name(...) { ... }` and `fn name(...) Error! { ... }` bare.

Error [E0121]: `s` was given away earlier, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/loop_stream_reuse.jet:12:15
    |
 12 |     loop x in s -> print("{x}")
    |               ^
 Why: after a value moves to another name, the old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: `s` is one-pass and cannot be copied — create a fresh source for the second drive

Error [E0107]: nothing named `x` exists here
  --> tests/ui/loop_stream_reuse.jet:12:28
    |
 12 |     loop x in s -> print("{x}")
    |                            ^
 Why: a name must be declared before it's used
 Fix: did you mean `s`?
